Program                                                  (10 Marks)
import java.io.*;
public class FileCopy2 {
public static void main(String[] args) {
try (
BufferedInputStream bis =
new BufferedInputStream(new FileInputStream("source.txt"));
BufferedOutputStream bos =
new BufferedOutputStream(new FileOutputStream("dest.txt"))
) {
byte[] buffer = new byte[1024];
int bytesRead;
while ((bytesRead = bis.read(buffer)) != -1) {
bos.write(buffer, 0, bytesRead);
}
bos.flush(); // Ensures all buffered data is written
System.out.println("Buffered file copy completed successfully.");
} catch (IOException e) {
System.out.println("Error while copying file.");
e.printStackTrace();
}       }    }
Explanation                                              (3 Marks)
The above Java program copies the contents of one file (source.txt) to another file (dest.txt) using BufferedInputStream and BufferedOutputStream.

